    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0593" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg505"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Newel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 379.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department transmits herewith a printed
                    copy of The Hague protocols.<anchor n="a" xml:id="d515-f1"/> Certified copies
                    are on the way from Venezuela and will be forwarded to you as soon as
                    received.</p>
                <p>The arbitrators have not yet been named. As soon as they are named you will
                    furnish, on behalf of Venezuela, to the International Bureau, a copy of these
                    protocols, with the request that the proper steps be taken for the installation
                    of the court. As soon as the Department is advised of the appointment of the
                    arbitrators, it will cable you their names, on receipt of which you will carry
                    out this instruction.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
